      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on the [[credential-scoping]] page, here\u0027s how the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment:\n\nThe Hub achieves this through **process environment isolation**:\n\n1. **No direct storage in Hub**: The Hub never holds the API key in its own process environment.\n\n2. **External source**: A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup (outside the Hub\u0027s environment).\n\n3. **Child-process injection**: The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes (like the Ingest and Query agents) immediately before they start \u2014 not the Hub\u0027s own environment.\n\n4. **Security benefit**: This means if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, an attacker cannot leak the credential by simply inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables. The key exists only transiently inside the short-lived child processes that actually need it.\n\nThis same scoping model applies to both the Ingest and Query agent processes \u2014 they each receive the credential via the same injection mechanism at their spawn time.",
